[h2]Build 0.9.19[/h2]
[h3]Changed[/h3]
[list]
[*]When a machine needs more than the network has (say 100 cloth with only 40 on the shelves), Loaders send the 40 and now say they are waiting for the rest, sending it as it turns up. Machines that can hold a part-filled job, like the repair center, keep what has arrived.
[*]A Feeder now tops up a part-full stack on a machine's spot or hopper with as much as fits, holding the remainder in its gripper until there is room, instead of waiting for the whole amount to fit at once.
[/list]
